  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The oxygen dissolved in water exerts a partial pressure of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kPa</mi></math> in the vapour above water. The molar solubility of oxygen in water is ______&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>dm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>(Round off to the Nearest Integer).</p><p>[Given : Henry&#39;s law constant&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kPa</mi></math>&nbsp;for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;Density of water with dissolved oxygen<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>dm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>]</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "1389",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></msub><mo>&#183;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math></p><p>or,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mtext>water&#160;</mtext></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>or,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4000</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mtext>water&#160;</mtext></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi>water</mi></msub></mfrac></math></p><p>Means <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> mole water <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>gm</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ml</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> dissolves</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4000</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;moles&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;Hence, molar solubility</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4000</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>18</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>72</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>dm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1388</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>89</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>dm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#8776;</mo><mn>1389</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>dm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math></p></blockquote>"
